# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Blostem Outreach — environment configuration
# Copy this file to ".env" (and ".env.local") and fill in the values you need.
# Most users only need DATABASE_URL — everything else is optional.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Database — PostgreSQL (works locally and on Vercel/serverless).
# On Vercel: add a Neon/Vercel Postgres store and this is set for you automatically.
# Locally: paste your Neon connection string (works from localhost too).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DB?sslmode=require"

# Optional: contact-finder search providers (set in Vercel env to enable the finder).
SERPER_API_KEY=""
GOOGLE_SEARCH_API_KEY=""

# Optional: stable secret for signing one-click unsubscribe links. If unset, one
# is generated and stored in the DB automatically. Set it in Vercel to keep
# unsubscribe links valid across redeploys.
UNSUBSCRIBE_SECRET=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel deploy notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Add a Postgres database (Vercel Storage -> Neon) — it sets the connection
#    string for you. Use the DIRECT (non-pooling) string as DATABASE_URL.
# 2. The build runs `prisma db push` to create tables automatically.
# 3. On Vercel the tunnel is disabled and the app's own https URL is used for
#    tracking/unsubscribe links (no cloudflared needed).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email open/click tracking (ALL OPTIONAL — tracking is automatic)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# By default the app auto-starts a free cloudflared "quick tunnel" on launch
# and detects its public URL itself. The user never has to paste a URL.
#
# Priority for the public tracking URL:
#   1) TRACKING_BASE_URL (below)
#   2) the auto cloudflared tunnel
#   3) the optional "Advanced custom host" field in Settings
#   4) none -> emails still send with working links, just no open/click stats
#
# --- Production hardening (stable URL that never rotates) ---
# Create a Cloudflare Named Tunnel, point a hostname (e.g. track.yourdomain.com)
# at http://localhost:3000, then set BOTH of these. Links in already-sent emails
# will never break because the URL is permanent.
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=""
# TRACKING_BASE_URL="https://track.yourdomain.com"

# --- Central server mode ---
# Point every copy you sell at one tracking host you operate. Set the URL and
# disable the local tunnel:
# TRACKING_BASE_URL="https://track.yourdomain.com"
# DISABLE_TUNNEL="1"

# --- Misc ---
# Turn the auto tunnel off entirely (tracking will use TRACKING_BASE_URL/manual):
# DISABLE_TUNNEL="1"
# Custom path to the cloudflared binary if it is not on PATH:
# CLOUDFLARED_PATH="C:\\Program Files (x86)\\cloudflared\\cloudflared.exe"
